claim.claim-text:
a computer processor;
a transceiver capable of communicating on a plurality of air-to-ground communication channels using at least one communication service;
the computer processor configured to cause the transceiver to allocate at least two communication channels to one communication service,
the computer processor configured to cause the transceiver to monitor the at least two communication channels for at least one source of interference, and the computer processor configured to cause the transceiver to avoid the at least one source of interference.

configuring a transceiver to schedule at least two air-to-ground communication channels to one communication service, wherein at least one of the communication services comprise a guard time where the transceiver halts transmission;
configuring the transceiver to monitor for at least one source of interference during the guard time; and
configuring the transceiver to avoid the at least one source of interference.
